# ---- est-13z1: the bead-close read-back gate (PR #360) ----
# `bead_close` is the SHIPPED PUBLIC GRAMMAR key and `bd -C <store> show <id> --json`
# is the runner's own enforcement argv — both are load-bearing public contract, the
# same GUARD class as the effect-receipt `effects` rows they mirror. The estate-vocab
# regex (`\bbd\b|\bbeads?\b`) fires on the contract naming; neutralizing it would ship
# a gate that names nothing. Line-anchored (not file-guarded): a future stray hit
# elsewhere in these files still fires. GUARD, per AGENTS.md rule 4.
# est-867 follow-up (main red at ee5018d): the est-13z1 and est-q2nwx/est-o8c6o
# hits were pinned by file:LINE and every later wf.py edit shifted them — the exact
# rot est-o8c6o already diagnosed. Re-anchored by FEATURE TOKEN per the playbook
# (a stray hit without a feature token still fires; the est-867 fixture proves it):
# bead/bd = the shipped public bead_close grammar naming; haus-docs = the joint-eng
# protocol citation surface (issue #174). GUARD, per AGENTS.md rule 4.
regex:bead
regex:\bbd\b
regex:est-13z1
regex:haus-docs
